//@version=6
// ============================================================================
//  DIRECTIONAL TIME FILTER  -  v1.7
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A time-boxed direction PERMISSION you can bolt onto any script. It only
//  answers "is a buy allowed now? is a sell allowed now?". Your script's own
//  entry and exit logic stays as it is; a signal that is not allowed is
//  simply not taken.
//
//  You say: "from THIS moment, for the next N minutes (countdown),
//            only take BUYS while PRICE is ABOVE the price of this moment
//            and only take SELLS while PRICE is BELOW it."
//  When the countdown reaches zero the filter closes: no new trades at all
//  until you activate it again.
//
//  THREE WAYS TO ARM IT
//    Direction signal  (automatic)  "Arm from signal" on: a direction signal
//                   coded inside the block (SIGNAL LOGIC SLOT) arms the
//                   filter on its bar: window from that bar's close, level
//                   = that bar's
//                   price, countdown runs, then closed until the next signal.
//                   Buys allowed only above the signal price, sells only
//                   below it. Works in backtests: committed bars only.
//                   "Signal logic" picks the signal:
//                     TDI cross (strategy)  default. The strategy's signal:
//                       TDI price line (SMA 2 of RSI 21) crosses ABOVE the
//                       signal line (SMA 7 of RSI 21) while it is above the
//                       market base line (SMA 34 of RSI 21) = BUY; crosses
//                       BELOW while below the base line = SELL. Level = the
//                       close of the cross bar. Calibrated on the strategy's
//                       BYBIT:BTCUSDT 2m export (2026-10-03..05): it fires on
//                       exactly the strategy's 35 Long and 50 Short bars,
//                       and on no other bar. (Export columns: "RSI Price
//                       Line" = SMA 2, "Fast Line" = SMA 7 = the signal
//                       line, "Middle Band" = SMA 34, "Slow Line" = the raw
//                       RSI 21; "Long Signal" / "Short Signal".)
//                     FlashGold v5  the v1.6 signal (RSI 14 TDI direction,
//                       parent + child zones, burst gate, entry hold).
//                       Level = its entry trigger (ask/bid +/- entry
//                       distance).
//                   The signal candle itself allows its own side AT the
//                   level (a buy at >= the level, a sell at <=), so the
//                   signal that armed the window passes it; every later
//                   candle needs price strictly beyond the level.
//    ACTIVATE NOW   (manual, one click)  Tick it, press OK. The window opens
//                   at that moment and the level is the price at that moment
//                   (or a price you type, see "Level when activating").
//                   Buys are allowed only above it, sells only below it, for
//                   the countdown. Start time and the manual levels are
//                   ignored. Untick + OK to disarm.
//                   While it stays ticked, ANY settings change or chart
//                   reload (refresh, symbol or timeframe change, more history
//                   loading, reconnect) activates it again at that moment and
//                   price: the status box shows "(NOW)" with the armed time
//                   and level so you always see what is armed. Use it when
//                   you are watching the chart. An alert created while it
//                   is ticked, or a strategy that reads this indicator
//                   through input.source (section B), runs its own copy and
//                   arms it when IT (re)loads; the box here shows only this
//                   copy. For those, use Start time.
//    Start time     (scheduled)  Date + minute (+ seconds) the window opens,
//                   with the manual price levels. Survives reloads; use it
//                   for anything left running or driven by alerts.
//
//  Example (ACTIVATE NOW at 14:30:00 with price 58.40, countdown 15):
//            14:30:00 -> 14:45:00   buy signals pass only if price > 58.40
//                                   sell signals pass only if price < 58.40
//            after 14:45:00         every signal is blocked
//
//  FILTER TIMEFRAME  (add-on, group "Filter timeframe (add-on)", off by
//  default)  Tick "Run the filter on" and pick a timeframe, say 1 hour: the
//  filter then runs on 1H candles whatever chart you look at. Set it up on
//  the 1H chart, switch the chart to 5m, 15m, 4H...: you keep seeing what
//  the filter sees on the 1H chart (same signals, levels, windows and
//  ALLOWED / BLOCKED). At any moment the answer is the one the 1H chart
//  gives at that same moment:
//    - the direction signal is computed on 1H candles with the selected
//      Signal logic (all its inputs, as on the 1H chart) and arms the
//      filter when its 1H candle closes, at that candle's level;
//    - a countdown in minutes runs on the clock: a 1H signal closing at
//      14:00 with countdown 15 is open 14:00 -> 14:15 on every chart;
//    - a countdown in candles counts 1H candles and covers the same 1H
//      candles as on the 1H chart (1 = only the signal candle, so on a 5m
//      chart only the 5m candle that closes with it: use minutes there);
//    - price is compared to the level as it moves, so a 5m chart judges
//      every 5m close: the 1H filter's verdict at that moment.
//  Only closed 1H candles are read, so nothing repaints: a 1H signal shows
//  on the chart candle that closes together with its 1H candle (on a higher
//  chart, on the candle that contains it). ACTIVATE NOW and Start time are
//  clock based and work as before; in Candles mode they count 1H candles
//  too. The status box title and the window labels show the timeframe in
//  use ("DTF 1H"). On the 1H chart itself the add-on changes nothing, and
//  unticked the filter runs on the chart's own candles exactly as v1.5.
//  On a lower chart the 1H history only starts where the chart's history
//  starts, so its first 1H candles are a warm-up (TDI, ATR) and can differ
//  from the 1H chart; later candles match it.
//
//  INPUTS (group "Directional time filter")
//    Enable filter      Off = every signal passes, as if the filter is absent.
//    ACTIVATE NOW       See above.
//    Level when activating   "Actual price": the level is the live price at
//                       the instant you press OK. "Typed price": the level
//                       is the number in "Typed price".
//    Start time         Scheduled start, chart time zone (minute precision;
//                       "+ seconds" adds seconds). Used when ACTIVATE NOW is
//                       off.
//    Countdown unit     Minutes, or Candles (chart candles counted from the
//                       candle that armed the window: 1 = that candle only;
//                       filter-timeframe candles when that add-on is on).
//    Countdown (min)    Minutes the window stays open from the start.
//                       0 = never expires.
//    Countdown (candles)  Candles the window stays open, in Candles mode.
//    Actual price       The live price ("Close" = last traded price of the
//                       current bar). ACTIVATE NOW captures it as the level
//                       and it is compared to the level in the window.
//    Buy only above     Manual buy level, used when ACTIVATE NOW is off.
//    Sell only below    Manual sell level, used when ACTIVATE NOW is off.
//    Allow buys/sells   Turn a side off completely inside the window.
//    Before start       What happens before the window opens:
//                       "Block" (no trades) or "Pass" (filter not active yet).
//    Shade window / Draw levels / Status box   Chart visuals.
//  INPUTS (group "Filter timeframe (add-on)")
//    Run the filter on  Off = the filter runs on this chart's candles. On =
//                       it runs on the timeframe next to it and this chart
//                       shows what it sees there. See FILTER TIMEFRAME.
//
//  OUTPUTS (Data Window / "Source" dropdown of another script)
//    DTF window open    1 while the window is open, 0 otherwise.
//    DTF buy allowed    1 when a buy may be taken on this bar, 0 otherwise.
//    DTF sell allowed   1 when a sell may be taken on this bar, 0 otherwise.
//    DTF expired        1 on the first bar after the window closes.
//    DTF price used     The series compared to the level (echo of Price).
//    DTF level          The level in force (armed price or manual buy level).
//
//  HOW TO USE IT
//  A) Paste into your own script (recommended)
//     Copy everything between the "BEGIN" and "END" markers below into your
//     script, below your own inputs. Then gate your entries:
//
//         if myBuySignal and dtfBuyOk
//             strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
//         if mySellSignal and dtfSellOk
//             strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
//
//     Exits are never gated. If your script runs in its own pane (a TDI,
//     an RSI...) set DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY = true so the visuals land on the
//     price chart. The block ships with the filter ON and nothing armed
//     (WAITING, everything blocked): activate it, or switch "Enable filter"
//     off until you need it.
//     To compare the level to one of your script's own series instead of
//     price, change  dtfValue = dtfRef  to  dtfValue = myLine  (myLine must
//     be computed above the block; move the block down if needed).
//
//  B) Link without editing (indicator -> strategy)
//     Add this indicator to the chart. In your strategy add
//         dtfBuyExt  = input.source(close, "DTF buy allowed")
//         dtfSellExt = input.source(close, "DTF sell allowed")
//     and in the strategy's settings pick the "DTF buy allowed" / "DTF sell
//     allowed" plots (listed under this indicator's name). Gate with
//         myBuySignal and dtfBuyExt == 1
//     (== 1, not > 0: if the plot is not linked the source is still 'close'
//     and must not count as allowed; a symbol that closes at exactly 1.0
//     would still slip through, so check the link in the settings.)
//     Use Start time in this setup: the strategy runs its own copy of the
//     indicator, and ACTIVATE NOW would arm that copy whenever the strategy
//     itself reloads, not when you press OK here.
//
//  TIMING
//  The committed value of every bar is judged at the bar's CLOSE time, on
//  history and live alike, so with Start time nothing changes when the chart
//  reloads and a strategy (which runs once per bar, at its close) backtests
//  exactly as it runs live; with ACTIVATE NOW the whole window moves to the
//  reload moment. A bar is inside the window when its close is in
//  [start, end): the bar that closes exactly at the start is inside (its
//  order fills at the start), the bar that closes exactly at the end is
//  outside. The order of the last allowed bar fills at the open of the
//  following bar; on a thinly traded symbol that can be after the window
//  has ended. While the live bar is still forming, the real clock is used,
//  so in an indicator the shading, status box and alerts open/close on the
//  exact second; those intrabar states are not kept once the bar closes.
//  A countdown shorter than one chart bar opens for at most one bar, maybe
//  none. On chart types without a close time (Renko, Kagi, Line Break,
//  Point & Figure) a bar is judged at its open time. Bar Replay: with Start
//  time, committed bars are right while the forming bar and the status box
//  follow the real clock, not the replay; ACTIVATE NOW also uses the real
//  clock, so it cannot be rehearsed in Replay. Alerts and webhook/broker
//  connections are
//  snapshots of the inputs at creation time: after changing them, re-create
//  the alert.
// ============================================================================
indicator("Directional Time Filter", "DTF", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500)

// ======================= BEGIN DIRECTIONAL TIME FILTER =======================
// Set true when this block lives in a script that runs in its own pane
// (overlay=false) so the visuals are drawn on the price chart.
DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY = false
// Set false when dtfValue is not a price (an oscillator), so the status box
// does not round the level to the symbol's tick.
DTF_LEVEL_IS_PRICE = true
GRP_DTF = "Directional time filter"
dtfOn        = input.bool(true, "Enable filter", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Off: every signal passes. On: closed at all times except the window a direction signal opens (or ACTIVATE NOW / Start time): then buys are allowed only above the level, sells only below it.")
dtfArmNow    = input.bool(false, "ACTIVATE NOW", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Tick and press OK: the window opens at this moment and the level is the price at this moment. Start time and the manual levels are ignored. Untick + OK to disarm. While ticked, ANY settings change or chart reload activates it again at that moment and price (the status box shows what is armed). Not for alerts or for strategies linked through input.source: use Start time for those.")
dtfLvMode    = input.string("Actual price", "Level when activating", options=["Actual price", "Typed price"], group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Actual price: ACTIVATE NOW captures the live price at that instant as the level. Typed price: the level is the number below.")
dtfTyped     = input.float(0, "Typed price", minval=0, group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="The level used by ACTIVATE NOW when 'Level when activating' is 'Typed price'. Buys allowed only above it, sells only below it.")
dtfStart     = input.time(timestamp("2030-01-01T00:00:00+0000"), "Start time", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Scheduled start, used when ACTIVATE NOW is off. Date and minute in the chart's time zone (the one on the time axis); add seconds below.")
dtfStartSec  = input.int(0, "+ seconds", minval=0, maxval=59, group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Seconds added to Start time (useful on second charts).")
dtfDurUnit   = input.string("Minutes", "Countdown unit", options=["Minutes", "Candles"], group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Minutes: the window stays open for the minutes below. Candles: the window stays open for the number of chart candles below, counted from the candle that armed it (1 = only that candle, whose order fills on the next one). With the Filter timeframe add-on on, the candles are that timeframe's.")
dtfMinutes   = input.float(15, "Countdown (minutes)", minval=0, step=1, group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Minutes the window stays open from the start. 0 = never expires. Bars are judged at their close, so a countdown shorter than one chart bar opens for at most one bar.")
dtfBars      = input.int(1, "Countdown (candles)", minval=1, group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Chart candles the window stays open, counted from the candle that armed it (filter-timeframe candles when that add-on is on).")
dtfRef       = input.source(close, "Actual price", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="The actual price: 'Close' is the last traded price of the current bar (it moves with every tick). ACTIVATE NOW captures this value as the level, and it is compared to the level while the window is open. The dropdown names are TradingView's; leave it on Close unless you want another series.")
dtfBuyLevel  = input.float(50, "Buy only above (manual)", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Manual buy level, used when ACTIVATE NOW is off. Buys are allowed only while price is above it.")
dtfSellLevel = input.float(50, "Sell only below (manual)", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Manual sell level, used when ACTIVATE NOW is off. Sells are allowed only while price is below it.")
dtfAllowBuy  = input.bool(true, "Allow buys", inline="side", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Turn one side off completely inside the window.")
dtfAllowSell = input.bool(true, "Allow sells", inline="side", group=GRP_DTF)
dtfBefore    = input.string("Block", "Before start", options=["Block", "Pass"], group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Block: nothing is allowed before the window opens. Pass: everything is allowed until the window opens.")
dtfShowBg    = input.bool(true, "Shade window", inline="vis", group=GRP_DTF)
dtfShowLv    = input.bool(true, "Draw level", inline="vis", group=GRP_DTF)
dtfShowTbl   = input.bool(true, "Status box", inline="vis", group=GRP_DTF, tooltip="Shown while the filter is enabled. Updates on each tick (once per bar inside a strategy) and freezes when the market is closed.")
dtfTblPos    = input.string("top_right", "Status box position", options=["top_right","middle_right","bottom_right","top_left","middle_left","bottom_left","top_center","bottom_center"], group=GRP_DTF)

// ---- Filter timeframe (add-on): run the filter on another timeframe ---------
GRP_PRJ  = "Filter timeframe (add-on)"
dtfPrjOn = input.bool(false, "Run the filter on", inline="prj", group=GRP_PRJ)
dtfPrjTf = input.timeframe("60", "", inline="prj", group=GRP_PRJ, tooltip="Off: the filter runs on this chart's candles. On: it runs on this timeframe and any chart shows what it sees there: the same signals, levels, windows and ALLOWED / BLOCKED as the filter on that timeframe's own chart, at the same moment. Set it on 1 hour, switch the chart to 5m or 4H, and you keep the 1H view. Only closed candles of that timeframe are read, so nothing repaints. On that timeframe's own chart it changes nothing.")

// ---- Direction signal: arms the filter automatically ------------------------
GRP_SIG = "Direction signal (arms the filter)"
dtfSigOn    = input.bool(true, "Arm from signal", group=GRP_SIG, tooltip="On: every direction signal arms the filter: the window opens on the signal bar, the level is the signal price, and the countdown runs. Buys are then allowed only above that price, sells only below it. ACTIVATE NOW (if ticked) has priority; Start time is ignored.")
dtfSigSide  = input.string("Buy and sell signals", "Arm on", options=["Buy and sell signals", "Buy signals only", "Sell signals only"], group=GRP_SIG)
dtfSigRearm = input.bool(true, "New signal re-arms while open", group=GRP_SIG, tooltip="On: a new signal inside an open window restarts it at the new price and time. Off: signals are ignored until the countdown ends.")
dtfSigMark  = input.bool(true, "Mark signal bars", group=GRP_SIG)

dtfValue  = dtfRef
dtfByBars = dtfDurUnit == "Candles"

// ===== SIGNAL LOGIC SLOT ======================================================
// Two direction signals, picked by "Signal logic". Orders, exits and sizing
// are NOT here: this only decides direction. It lives in dtfSignal(ctxSec),
// which returns [buy signal, sell signal, signal price]: it runs on the
// chart, and on the filter timeframe when that add-on is on (ctxSec = seconds
// of the timeframe it runs on, so "the chart" in the tooltips below means
// that timeframe). To arm from your own logic, replace the body of dtfSignal
// and keep what it returns.
gSig = "Signal logic"
sigLogic = input.string("TDI cross (strategy)", "Signal logic", options = ["TDI cross (strategy)", "FlashGold v5"], group = gSig, tooltip = "TDI cross (strategy): the strategy's signal, calibrated on its export: the TDI price line crosses the signal line on the side of the market base line. FlashGold v5: the v1.6 signal (TDI direction, zones, burst gate, entry hold). Each logic only uses its own group of inputs below.")

// ---- TDI cross (strategy) ---------------------------------------------------
// The TDI of the strategy: RSI 21 of close; price line = SMA 2 of it, signal
// line = SMA 7, market base line = SMA 34. BUY when the price line crosses
// above the signal line while above the base line; SELL when it crosses below
// while below the base line. Level = the close of the cross bar.
gTdiX = "TDI cross (strategy)"
tdiXRsiLen   = input.int(21, "RSI length", minval = 2, group = gTdiX)
tdiXPriceLen = input.int(2, "Price line, SMA of RSI", minval = 1, group = gTdiX)
tdiXSigLen   = input.int(7, "Signal line, SMA of RSI", minval = 1, group = gTdiX)
tdiXBaseLen  = input.int(34, "Market base line, SMA of RSI", minval = 1, group = gTdiX)
tdiXUseBase  = input.bool(true, "Buy only above the base line, sell only below", group = gTdiX, tooltip = "On (the strategy): a cross counts only on the side of the market base line. Off: every cross of the price line and the signal line is a signal.")

tdiCrossSignal() =>
    float xRsi   = ta.rsi(close, tdiXRsiLen)
    float xPrice = ta.sma(xRsi, tdiXPriceLen)
    float xSig   = ta.sma(xRsi, tdiXSigLen)
    float xBase  = ta.sma(xRsi, tdiXBaseLen)
    bool  xBuy   = ta.crossover(xPrice, xSig) and (not tdiXUseBase or xPrice > xBase)
    bool  xSell  = ta.crossunder(xPrice, xSig) and (not tdiXUseBase or xPrice < xBase)
    [xBuy, xSell, close]

// ---- FlashGold Continuation v5 direction ------------------------------------
// The direction logic of "FlashGold Continuation v5 - TDI Trade Zone Filter"
// (© ghostsmartfire), as in the FlashGold v5 strategy: bid/ask model, TDI
// direction (RSI -> SMA fast / slow, fast rising = BUY), parent + six child
// zones alignment, burst gate, prior-drift filter, entry hold, one signal per
// bar.
gCore = "FlashGold Core"
spreadPoints          = input.float(25.0, "Spread pts", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore, tooltip = "Full spread in points (mintick units). Half of it offsets bid and ask.")
entryDistPoints       = input.float(50.0, "Entry distance pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore)
entryHoldBars         = input.int(0, "Entry hold bars", minval = 0, group = gCore)
entryHoldMinFavPoints = input.float(5.0, "Hold min favorable pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gCore)
oneEntryPerBar        = input.bool(true, "One signal per bar", group = gCore)

gBurst = "Burst / Direction"
DistUnit         = input.string("ATR", "Burst / entry distance / hold unit", options = ["ATR", "Points"], group = gBurst, tooltip = "ATR: the three thresholds below are multiples of ATR(14) of the chart. Points: the point inputs in the Core group are used.")
burstAtrMult     = input.float(0.5, "Burst threshold, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
entryDistAtrMult = input.float(0.25, "Entry distance, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
holdFavAtrMult   = input.float(0.1, "Hold min favorable, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gBurst)
burstPointsInput = input.float(172.0, "Burst threshold pts (Points unit)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = gBurst)
useBurstGate     = input.bool(true, "Require burst gate", group = gBurst)
useAnyCombo      = input.bool(false, "Allow any combo", group = gBurst, tooltip = "If on, TDI parent/zone can approve direction even when burst is weaker.")
priorDriftBars   = input.int(60, "Prior drift bars", minval = 1, group = gBurst)
usePriorFilter   = input.bool(false, "Use prior drift filter", group = gBurst)

gZone = "TDI Trade Zone Filter"
useTdiTradeZone = input.bool(true, "Use TDI trade-zone filter", group = gZone)
tdiParentTf     = input.timeframe("60", "Parent obedience timeframe", group = gZone, tooltip = "Calibrated with the parent = the chart timeframe. Leave it equal to the chart.")
tdiRsiLen       = input.int(14, "TDI RSI length", minval = 2, group = gZone)
tdiFastLen      = input.int(2, "TDI white fast length", minval = 1, group = gZone)
tdiSlowLen      = input.int(7, "TDI slow length", minval = 1, group = gZone)
minAlignedZones = input.int(2, "Minimum child zones aligned", minval = 0, maxval = 6, group = gZone)
allowNeutralParent = input.bool(false, "Allow trade if parent is flat", group = gZone)
ignoreNaZones   = input.bool(true, "Ignore zones without data", group = gZone, tooltip = "A child zone whose timeframe has no data on this bar is dropped from the active count instead of counting as MIX.")
htfNoRepaint    = input.bool(true, "Higher-TF zones use the last CLOSED bar", group = gZone, tooltip = "A child zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the chart is read from its last closed bar, so history and realtime agree.")
useZone1 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 1", group = gZone)
zoneTf1  = input.timeframe("60", "Zone 1 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone2 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 2", group = gZone)
zoneTf2  = input.timeframe("120", "Zone 2 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone3 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 3", group = gZone)
zoneTf3  = input.timeframe("240", "Zone 3 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone4 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 4", group = gZone)
zoneTf4  = input.timeframe("480", "Zone 4 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone5 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 5", group = gZone)
zoneTf5  = input.timeframe("1", "Zone 5 timeframe", group = gZone)
useZone6 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 6", group = gZone)
zoneTf6  = input.timeframe("2", "Zone 6 timeframe", group = gZone)

// TDI direction
tdiDir() =>
    r = ta.rsi(close, tdiRsiLen)
    f = ta.sma(r, tdiFastLen)
    s = ta.sma(r, tdiSlowLen)
    d = f > f[1] ? 1 : f < f[1] ? -1 : 0
    [d, f, s]

tdiDirPrev() =>
    [d, f, s] = tdiDir()
    [d[1], f[1], s[1]]

// Direction of a child zone. A zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the one the
// signal runs on (ctxSec) is read from its last closed bar (htfNoRepaint).
zoneDir(string tf, int ctxSec) =>
    [zD0, zF0, zS0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
    [zDP, zFP, zSP] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, tdiDirPrev(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
    htfNoRepaint and timeframe.in_seconds(tf) > ctxSec ? zDP : zD0

zoneOn(bool use, int dir) =>
    use and (not ignoreNaZones or not na(dir))

alignCount(int dir, bool useZone, int side) =>
    useZone and side != 0 and dir == side ? 1 : 0

fgSignal(int ctxSec) =>
    // price model
    pt = syminfo.mintick
    halfSpread = spreadPoints * pt * 0.5
    bid = close - halfSpread
    ask = close + halfSpread
    midPrice = (bid + ask) * 0.5

    [parentDir, parentFast, parentSlow] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tdiParentTf, tdiDir(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
    z1Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf1, ctxSec)
    z2Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf2, ctxSec)
    z3Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf3, ctxSec)
    z4Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf4, ctxSec)
    z5Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf5, ctxSec)
    z6Dir = zoneDir(zoneTf6, ctxSec)

    on1 = zoneOn(useZone1, z1Dir)
    on2 = zoneOn(useZone2, z2Dir)
    on3 = zoneOn(useZone3, z3Dir)
    on4 = zoneOn(useZone4, z4Dir)
    on5 = zoneOn(useZone5, z5Dir)
    on6 = zoneOn(useZone6, z6Dir)

    activeZones = (on1 ? 1 : 0) + (on2 ? 1 : 0) + (on3 ? 1 : 0) + (on4 ? 1 : 0) + (on5 ? 1 : 0) + (on6 ? 1 : 0)
    parentSide = parentDir > 0 ? 1 : parentDir < 0 ? -1 : 0

    alignedZones = alignCount(z1Dir, on1, parentSide) + alignCount(z2Dir, on2, parentSide) + alignCount(z3Dir, on3, parentSide) + alignCount(z4Dir, on4, parentSide) + alignCount(z5Dir, on5, parentSide) + alignCount(z6Dir, on6, parentSide)

    requiredAligned = math.min(minAlignedZones, activeZones)
    parentFlatAllowed = allowNeutralParent and parentSide == 0
    zoneReady = activeZones == 0 or alignedZones >= requiredAligned

    tradeZoneBuyAllowed = not useTdiTradeZone or ((parentSide == 1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)
    tradeZoneSellAllowed = not useTdiTradeZone or ((parentSide == -1 or parentFlatAllowed) and zoneReady)

    // burst / prior drift
    atrChart = ta.atr(14)
    atrPts = atrChart / pt
    burstThrPts   = DistUnit == "ATR" ? burstAtrMult * atrPts : burstPointsInput
    entryDistPts  = DistUnit == "ATR" ? entryDistAtrMult * atrPts : entryDistPoints
    holdFavPts    = DistUnit == "ATR" ? holdFavAtrMult * atrPts : entryHoldMinFavPoints

    burstPts = (midPrice - midPrice[1]) / pt
    priorDriftPts = (midPrice - midPrice[priorDriftBars]) / pt

    burstBuy = burstPts >= burstThrPts
    burstSell = burstPts <= -burstThrPts

    priorBuyOk = not usePriorFilter or priorDriftPts > 0
    priorSellOk = not usePriorFilter or priorDriftPts < 0

    rawBuyCandidate = useAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and (not useBurstGate or burstBuy or parentSide == 1)) : (tradeZoneBuyAllowed and burstBuy)
    rawSellCandidate = useAnyCombo ? (tradeZoneSellAllowed and (not useBurstGate or burstSell or parentSide == -1)) : (tradeZoneSellAllowed and burstSell)

    buyCandidate = rawBuyCandidate and priorBuyOk
    sellCandidate = rawSellCandidate and priorSellOk

    // entry hold / virtual stop
    var bool holdActive = false
    var bool holdIsBuy = false
    var int holdSignalBar = na
    var float holdSignalMid = na
    var int lastEntryBar = na

    float buyEntryPrice = na
    float sellEntryPrice = na
    bool buySignal = false
    bool sellSignal = false

    canFire = not oneEntryPerBar or na(lastEntryBar) or lastEntryBar != bar_index

    if buyCandidate and canFire
        if entryHoldBars == 0
            buyEntryPrice := ask + entryDistPts * pt
            buySignal := true
            lastEntryBar := bar_index
        else if not holdActive
            holdActive := true
            holdIsBuy := true
            holdSignalBar := bar_index
            holdSignalMid := midPrice
        else if holdIsBuy
            elapsedBars = bar_index - holdSignalBar
            holdMovePoints = (midPrice - holdSignalMid) / pt
            if elapsedBars >= entryHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
                buyEntryPrice := ask + entryDistPts * pt
                buySignal := true
                lastEntryBar := bar_index
                holdActive := false

    if sellCandidate and canFire
        if entryHoldBars == 0
            sellEntryPrice := bid - entryDistPts * pt
            sellSignal := true
            lastEntryBar := bar_index
        else if not holdActive
            holdActive := true
            holdIsBuy := false
            holdSignalBar := bar_index
            holdSignalMid := midPrice
        else if not holdIsBuy
            elapsedBars = bar_index - holdSignalBar
            holdMovePoints = (holdSignalMid - midPrice) / pt
            if elapsedBars >= entryHoldBars and holdMovePoints >= holdFavPts
                sellEntryPrice := bid - entryDistPts * pt
                sellSignal := true
                lastEntryBar := bar_index
                holdActive := false

    if holdActive and ((holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneBuyAllowed) or (not holdIsBuy and not tradeZoneSellAllowed))
        holdActive := false
        holdSignalBar := na
        holdSignalMid := na

    // The level is the strategy's entry trigger price (ask/bid +/- entry distance).
    float signalPx = buySignal ? buyEntryPrice : sellSignal ? sellEntryPrice : na
    [buySignal, sellSignal, signalPx]

// The direction signal of the selected logic. Both logics are computed on
// every bar (Pine wants ta.* calls on every bar; "Signal logic" is an input,
// so the choice is fixed for the run); only the selected one is returned.
dtfSignal(int ctxSec) =>
    [fgBuy, fgSell, fgPx] = fgSignal(ctxSec)
    [txBuy, txSell, txPx] = tdiCrossSignal()
    bool useFg = sigLogic == "FlashGold v5"
    [useFg ? fgBuy : txBuy, useFg ? fgSell : txSell, useFg ? fgPx : txPx]

// The chart's own direction signal.
[dtfBuySignal, dtfSellSignal, dtfSignalPx] = dtfSignal(timeframe.in_seconds())
// ===== END SIGNAL LOGIC SLOT ==================================================

// Signal arming, on the timeframe it runs on: a confirmed signal bar arms
// the window at that bar's close with the level at the signal price.
// Committed state only (var), so backtests and live agree. 'confirmed' is
// barstate.isconfirmed on the chart; true on the filter timeframe, where only
// closed candles are ever read. aId counts the arms.
dtfArm(bool sBuy, bool sSell, float sPx, float px, bool confirmed) =>
    var int   aAt  = na
    var int   aBar = na
    var float aPx  = na
    var int   aDir = 0
    var int   aId  = 0
    int  aClose = nz(time_close, time)
    bool aEnded = na(aAt) or (dtfByBars ? bar_index >= aBar + dtfBars : (dtfMinutes > 0 and aClose >= aAt + math.round(dtfMinutes * 60000)))
    bool aFire  = dtfSigOn and confirmed and not na(px) and ((sBuy and dtfSigSide != "Sell signals only") or (sSell and dtfSigSide != "Buy signals only")) and (aEnded or dtfSigRearm)
    if aFire
        aAt  := aClose
        aBar := bar_index
        aPx  := nz(sPx, px)
        aDir := sBuy ? 1 : -1
        aId  += 1
    [aFire, aAt, aBar, aPx, aDir, aId]

[dtfSigFire0, dtfSigAt0, dtfSigBar0, dtfSigPx0, dtfSigDir0, dtfSigId0] = dtfArm(dtfBuySignal, dtfSellSignal, dtfSignalPx, dtfValue, barstate.isconfirmed)

// Filter timeframe (add-on): the signal and its arming run on that
// timeframe. Each of its candles sends its arm, the arm of the candle before
// it, and its index, open and close time. An arm is used only once the
// candle that made it has closed by this chart's clock, so the forming
// filter candle is never read and nothing repaints.
dtfPrjRead() =>
    [pBuy, pSell, pSigPx] = dtfSignal(timeframe.in_seconds(dtfPrjTf))
    [pFire, pAt, pBar, pPx, pDir, pId] = dtfArm(pBuy, pSell, pSigPx, close, true)
    [pAt, pBar, pPx, pDir, pId, bar_index, time, nz(time_close, time), pAt[1], pBar[1], pPx[1], pDir[1], pId[1]]

bool dtfPrj = dtfPrjOn and timeframe.in_seconds(dtfPrjTf) != timeframe.in_seconds()
[dpAt, dpBar, dpPx, dpDir, dpId, dpIdx, dpOpen, dpClose, dqAt, dqBar, dqPx, dqDir, dqId] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, dtfPrjTf, dtfPrjRead(), barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)

dtfTfText(string tf) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    sec < 60 ? str.tostring(sec) + "s" : sec < 3600 ? str.tostring(sec / 60, "#.##") + "m" : sec < 86400 ? str.tostring(sec / 3600, "#.##") + "H" : tf
string dtfTfTag = dtfPrj ? " " + dtfTfText(dtfPrjTf) : ""

// Clock. The committed value of a bar (history, and the closing update of the
// live bar) is judged at the bar's close time, so it never repaints. Intrabar
// ticks of the live bar use the real clock, so the window opens on the second.
dtfClock = barstate.isconfirmed ? nz(time_close, time) : timenow

// The arm in force: the chart's own, or (add-on) the latest filter candle's
// once it has closed by this clock, else the candle before it.
bool  dtfPrjDone = dtfClock >= dpClose
int   dtfSigAt   = dtfPrj ? (dtfPrjDone ? dpAt  : dqAt)  : dtfSigAt0
int   dtfSigBar  = dtfPrj ? (dtfPrjDone ? dpBar : dqBar) : dtfSigBar0
float dtfSigPx   = dtfPrj ? (dtfPrjDone ? dpPx  : dqPx)  : dtfSigPx0
int   dtfSigDir  = dtfPrj ? nz(dtfPrjDone ? dpDir : dqDir) : dtfSigDir0
int   dtfSigId   = dtfPrj ? (dtfPrjDone ? dpId  : dqId)  : dtfSigId0
// Add-on: a new arm shows on the chart candle where it becomes known (on a
// higher chart, one mark for all the filter candles it contains).
bool  dtfSigFire = dtfPrj ? (not na(dtfSigId[1]) and nz(dtfSigId) > dtfSigId[1]) : dtfSigFire0
// The candle being judged, for Candles mode: the chart candle, or (add-on)
// the filter candle this clock falls in; one closing exactly at the clock is
// the one judged, as on its own chart, where a candle is judged at its close.
int   dtfIdx     = not dtfPrj ? bar_index : dtfClock <= dpOpen ? dpIdx - 1 : dtfClock <= dpClose ? dpIdx : dpIdx + 1

// ACTIVATE NOW capture: the moment and the price when the script (re)starts
// with the switch on. varip keeps it across live updates; a recompile (any
// settings change, chart reload) captures again.
varip int   dtfArmedAt  = na
varip float dtfArmedPx  = na
varip int   dtfArmedBar = na
// The capture waits for a tick where the price source has a value.
if dtfArmNow and barstate.islast and na(dtfArmedAt) and not na(dtfValue)
    dtfArmedAt  := timenow
    dtfArmedBar := dtfIdx
    dtfArmedPx := dtfLvMode == "Typed price" ? dtfTyped : dtfValue

dtfStartAt = dtfArmNow ? dtfArmedAt : dtfSigOn ? dtfSigAt : dtfStart + dtfStartSec * 1000
dtfEnd     = not dtfByBars and dtfMinutes > 0 and not na(dtfStartAt) ? dtfStartAt + math.round(dtfMinutes * 60000) : na
dtfOneLv   = dtfArmNow or dtfSigOn
dtfBuyLv   = dtfArmNow ? dtfArmedPx : dtfSigOn ? dtfSigPx : dtfBuyLevel
dtfSellLv  = dtfArmNow ? dtfArmedPx : dtfSigOn ? dtfSigPx : dtfSellLevel

// Not armed yet (ACTIVATE NOW before the capture bar) counts as before start.
dtfBeforeStart = na(dtfStartAt) or dtfClock < dtfStartAt
// Candle mode: the window is the N candles from the one that armed it. For a
// scheduled start that is the first candle closing at or after Start time.
var int dtfTimeBar = na
if not dtfBeforeStart and na(dtfTimeBar)
    dtfTimeBar := dtfIdx
if dtfBeforeStart
    dtfTimeBar := na
int  dtfStartBar = dtfArmNow ? dtfArmedBar : dtfSigOn ? dtfSigBar : dtfTimeBar
int  dtfEndBar   = na(dtfStartBar) ? na : dtfStartBar + dtfBars
bool dtfInBars   = dtfByBars and not na(dtfEndBar) and dtfIdx < dtfEndBar
dtfOpen        = not dtfBeforeStart and (dtfByBars ? dtfInBars : (na(dtfEnd) or dtfClock < dtfEnd))
dtfAfterEnd    = dtfByBars ? (not dtfBeforeStart and not dtfInBars) : (not na(dtfEnd) and dtfClock >= dtfEnd)

// The candle that a signal armed on: its price IS the level (TDI cross), so
// there it counts as at the level on the signal's own side, and the signal
// that armed the window passes it. The other side still needs to be beyond.
bool dtfOnSigBar = dtfSigOn and not dtfArmNow and not na(dtfStartBar) and dtfIdx == dtfStartBar
bool dtfAtBuyLv  = dtfOnSigBar and dtfSigDir > 0 and dtfValue >= dtfBuyLv
bool dtfAtSellLv = dtfOnSigBar and dtfSigDir < 0 and dtfValue <= dtfSellLv

// Final gates: is a buy / a sell ALLOWED on this bar? (Permission only.)
dtfBuyOk  = not dtfOn or (dtfBeforeStart and dtfBefore == "Pass") or (dtfOpen and dtfAllowBuy  and (dtfValue > dtfBuyLv  or dtfAtBuyLv))
dtfSellOk = not dtfOn or (dtfBeforeStart and dtfBefore == "Pass") or (dtfOpen and dtfAllowSell and (dtfValue < dtfSellLv or dtfAtSellLv))

// True on the first bar after the window has closed (chart marker / output).
dtfExpired = dtfOn and dtfAfterEnd and not dtfAfterEnd[1] and not barstate.isfirst

// A countdown shorter than one chart bar opens for at most one bar.
dtfTooShort = dtfOn and not dtfByBars and dtfMinutes > 0 and dtfMinutes * 60 < timeframe.in_seconds()

// ---- Visuals (optional: delete from here to END if you only want the gates)
dtfPosOf(string s) =>
    switch s
        "top_right"     => position.top_right
        "bottom_right"  => position.bottom_right
        "top_left"      => position.top_left
        "middle_left"   => position.middle_left
        "bottom_left"   => position.bottom_left
        "top_center"    => position.top_center
        "bottom_center" => position.bottom_center
        => position.middle_right

bgcolor(dtfShowBg and dtfOn and dtfOpen ? (dtfBuyOk and dtfSellOk ? color.new(color.yellow, 85) : dtfBuyOk ? color.new(color.green, 85) : dtfSellOk ? color.new(color.red, 85) : color.new(color.gray, 88)) : na, title="DTF window", force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(dtfExpired, "DTF window ended", shape.xcross, location.top, color.orange, size=size.tiny, text="DTF end", textcolor=color.orange, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(dtfSigMark and dtfSigFire and dtfSigDir > 0, "DTF buy signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.lime, size=size.tiny, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
plotshape(dtfSigMark and dtfSigFire and dtfSigDir < 0, "DTF sell signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.red,  size=size.tiny, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)

// Level lines as drawings (they do not stretch the price scale). Each window
// keeps its own line and a label at its start, so past windows stay readable.
// While waiting (manual / scheduled modes) the line previews the last 50 bars.
// Redrawn every bar so a host script's own drawings never garbage-collect the
// current one.
dtfActive = dtfOn and (dtfBeforeStart or dtfOpen) and not na(dtfBuyLv)
var line  dtfBuyLn    = na
var line  dtfSellLn   = na
var label dtfLbl      = na
var int   dtfOpenFrom = na
bool dtfNewWindow = dtfOpen and na(dtfOpenFrom)
if dtfNewWindow
    dtfOpenFrom := bar_index
    // a new window: leave the previous window's drawings in place
    dtfBuyLn  := na
    dtfSellLn := na
    dtfLbl    := na
if dtfShowLv and dtfActive
    int dtfX1 = math.max(0, math.max(bar_index - 9000, math.min(dtfOpen ? dtfOpenFrom : bar_index, bar_index - 50)))
    line.delete(dtfBuyLn)
    line.delete(dtfSellLn)
    if dtfOneLv
        color dtfLnCol = dtfSigOn and dtfSigDir > 0 ? color.lime : dtfSigOn and dtfSigDir < 0 ? color.red : color.white
        dtfBuyLn := line.new(dtfX1, dtfBuyLv, bar_index, dtfBuyLv, color=dtfLnCol, width=2, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
    else
        dtfBuyLn  := line.new(dtfX1, dtfBuyLv,  bar_index, dtfBuyLv,  color=color.new(color.green, 0), width=2, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
        dtfSellLn := line.new(dtfX1, dtfSellLv, bar_index, dtfSellLv, color=color.new(color.red, 0),   width=2, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
    if dtfOpen and na(dtfLbl)
        string dtfWhat = dtfArmNow ? "NOW" : dtfSigOn ? (dtfSigDir > 0 ? "SIGNAL BUY" : "SIGNAL SELL") + dtfTfTag : "START"
        string dtfTxt  = dtfWhat + " @ " + str.tostring(dtfBuyLv, DTF_LEVEL_IS_PRICE ? format.mintick : "#.########") + (dtfByBars ? "\n" + str.tostring(dtfBars) + (dtfBars == 1 ? " candle" : " candles") + dtfTfTag : dtfMinutes > 0 ? "\n" + str.tostring(dtfMinutes, "#.#") + " min" : "\nno limit")
        color  dtfLbCol = dtfSigOn and dtfSigDir < 0 ? color.new(color.red, 20) : dtfSigOn and dtfSigDir > 0 ? color.new(color.lime, 20) : color.new(color.white, 20)
        dtfLbl := label.new(dtfOpenFrom, dtfBuyLv, dtfTxt, style=label.style_label_right, color=dtfLbCol, textcolor=color.black, size=size.small, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
else if not dtfActive
    dtfOpenFrom := na

// Status box, judged by the real clock (display only; the gates never use it).
var table dtfTable = table.new(dtfPosOf(dtfTblPos), 2, 7, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), border_width=1, force_overlay=DTF_FORCE_OVERLAY)
if dtfShowTbl and dtfOn and barstate.islast
    bool   dBefore = na(dtfStartAt) or timenow < dtfStartAt
    bool   dAfter  = dtfByBars ? (not dBefore and not dtfInBars) : (not na(dtfEnd) and timenow >= dtfEnd)
    bool   dOpen   = not dBefore and not dAfter
    bool   dBuy    = (dBefore and dtfBefore == "Pass") or (dOpen and dtfAllowBuy  and (dtfValue > dtfBuyLv  or dtfAtBuyLv))
    bool   dSell   = (dBefore and dtfBefore == "Pass") or (dOpen and dtfAllowSell and (dtfValue < dtfSellLv or dtfAtSellLv))
    string dMode   = dtfArmNow ? " (NOW)" : dtfSigOn ? (dtfSigDir > 0 ? " (SIGNAL BUY)" : dtfSigDir < 0 ? " (SIGNAL SELL)" : " (SIGNAL)") : ""
    string dState  = (dBefore ? (dtfTooShort ? "WAITING (< 1 bar)" : "WAITING") : dOpen ? "OPEN" : "ENDED") + dMode
    color  dCol    = dBefore ? color.yellow : dOpen ? color.lime : color.orange
    int    dSecs   = dOpen and not na(dtfEnd) ? math.max(0, math.floor((dtfEnd - timenow) / 1000.0)) : 0
    string dLeft   = dOpen and dtfByBars ? str.tostring(dtfEndBar - dtfIdx) + (dtfEndBar - dtfIdx == 1 ? " candle" : " candles") + dtfTfTag : dOpen and not na(dtfEnd) ? str.tostring(math.floor(dSecs / 60), "00") + ":" + str.tostring(dSecs % 60, "00") : dOpen ? "no limit" : "-"
    string dStart  = na(dtfStartAt) ? "-" : str.format_time(dtfStartAt, "MMM dd HH:mm:ss", syminfo.timezone)
    string dFmt    = DTF_LEVEL_IS_PRICE ? format.mintick : "#.########"
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 0, "DTF" + dtfTfTag, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 0, dState, text_color=dCol)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 1, "Now (exch tz)", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 1, str.format_time(timenow, "MMM dd HH:mm:ss", syminfo.timezone), text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 2, "Start (exch tz)", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 2, dStart, text_color=dtfArmNow ? color.orange : dtfSigOn ? color.aqua : color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 3, "Countdown", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 3, dLeft, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 4, "Price now", text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 4, na(dtfValue) ? "-" : str.tostring(dtfValue, dFmt), text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 5, "Buy  > " + (na(dtfBuyLv)  ? "-" : str.tostring(dtfBuyLv,  dFmt)), text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 5, dBuy ? "ALLOWED" : "BLOCKED", text_color=dBuy ? color.lime : color.red)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 0, 6, "Sell < " + (na(dtfSellLv) ? "-" : str.tostring(dtfSellLv, dFmt)), text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(dtfTable, 1, 6, dSell ? "ALLOWED" : "BLOCKED", text_color=dSell ? color.lime : color.red)
// ======================== END DIRECTIONAL TIME FILTER ========================

// Exported values (Data Window + linkable as a source from other scripts).
plot(dtfOn and dtfOpen ? 1 : 0, "DTF window open", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfBuyOk ? 1 : 0, "DTF buy allowed", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfSellOk ? 1 : 0, "DTF sell allowed", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfExpired ? 1 : 0, "DTF expired", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfValue, "DTF price used", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfBuyLv, "DTF level", display=display.data_window)
plot(dtfSigFire ? dtfSigDir : 0, "DTF signal (1 buy, -1 sell)", display=display.data_window)
